      "lineNbr": 8,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-30T21:09:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Are these GPIOs initialized anywhere?  The `gpio-keys` compatible C driver doesn\u0027t actually exist in Zephyr upstream.  Board that use this upstream generally use the node-label or an alias to find the GPIO pins to initialize.  You don\u0027t have any board code referencing anything in this file best I can tell.\n\nSo this file seems to be adding unused nodes into the devicetree.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 8,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 8,
        "endChar": 7
      },
      "revId": "8411ef8976a2caf233d0731fc5a78fbb6ffa2852",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1a88fb7d_921b634a",
        "filename": "zephyr/program/hdctools/starfish_v1/gpio.dts",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 8,
      "author": {
        "id": 1347380
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-31T01:39:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The next CLs initialize it. There\u0027s a macro GPIO_LIST_CTX() created which allows us to identify gpio and configure it based on the grouping patterns. The macro automatically creates a struct for each gpio within the blocks and assigns them GPIO_LABEL\u0027s and indexes based on the device tree. \n\nIt allows us to initialize each node with a statement like:\n\n    static struct button_ctx all_buttons[] \u003d { GPIO_LIST_CTX(button) };\n    static struct led_ctx all_leds[] \u003d { GPIO_LIST_CTX(led) };\n    static struct sim_ctx all_sim_gpios[] \u003d { GPIO_LIST_CTX(sim) };\n\nThat `struct gpio_ctx` is a small amount of RAM, but it\u0027s only 16 Bytes total leaving since I left everything at `int` defaults rather than `uint16_t`. All 28 calls are wasting less than 500 bytes of RAM out of the 120kB free. It can be optimized in a few different ways if we wanted it as a proper device tree driver but we\u0027re nowhere near limits on this project so resources can be spent elsewhere where it\u0027s needed.",
      "parentUuid": "a503d98b_ef3bed35",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 8,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 8,
        "endChar": 7
      },
      "revId": "8411ef8976a2caf233d0731fc5a78fbb6ffa2852",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
